Original commit body from ed4b9305d7b992c03dbd034b9f1581116372b1f3:

pytest exits 0 when every collected test skipped, and the Woodpecker
per-PR pytest step read only the exit code (it already failed exit 5,
"collected nothing", since INV-tazur). So a selection whose every test
skipped passed the gate while smart-test locally called the same run
ZERO TESTS EXECUTED. Reproduced before the fix by executing the real
step block through test_ci_pytest_selection_gate's harness with a stub
pytest printing "1 skipped" and exiting 0: the step exited 0.

The step now passes --junit-xml to pytest and, on exit 0, counts the
testcases that ran by smart-test's count_executed_tests rule: a skip does
not count, an xfail (junit reports it as a skip) does. Zero fails with
exit 5 and says so; no readable report fails closed (exit 1) -- the gate
cannot count, so it does not pass. A nonzero count is printed.

The counting snippet is inline, not shared with smart-test: smart-test's
own harness drives its functions extracted from the file, and the step
runs before anything is installed from scripts/. Two copies of the rule,
each pointing at the other's name.

Tests (the real block, driven): the stub pytest now writes the junit
report a test gives it (default: one passed testcase). New: all skipped
-> exit 5; one passed beside a skip -> exit 0 and the count printed; an
xfail alone -> exit 0; no report -> fails, named. Each asserts pytest ran
and was handed --junit-xml first. Mutation-checked: making the zero
branch or the no-report branch pass reds exactly its own test. The
extracted snippet reads a real xdist junit report (19 testcases).

Not changed: the dormant .github/workflows/ci.yml pytest job, which has
the same shape; GitHub Actions runs only release.yml.

Addresses INV-zuvij.

